From f3a14ef16c71e68a484ce835368a2966826a5e32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:06:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): usage accounts say why they are limited
 [daveey]

A limited account row only said 'limited': a temporary credential-wide
cooldown (generic 429, transient auth) looked the same as a spent quota.
Additive, sanitized fields on usage.accounts rows (classified codes and
timestamps only, never a provider message):

- limit_kind: quota (exhausted account window, billing, provider
  usage/quota reason such as Codex usage_limit_reached) or cooldown
- reason: quota_window / billing / usage_limit / rate_limit / auth / cooldown
- cooldown_until: ISO expiry of a live credential-wide cooldown
- model_cooldowns: live per-model cooldowns that leave the account usable
  (entitlement benches excluded)

state keeps its meaning (limited still blocks selection); the read path
still never writes auth.json. Contract + generated files updated.
